#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119887 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119707 :question/id #uuid "175c458d-36cc-5f90-b6ee-976e082c30a2" :question/math-academy-id "e-8943" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u^2, \\: v^2, \\: u+v \\big\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $\\mathbf r (u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v.$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2v & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2v,\\,-2u,\\,4uv⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "df6cef5e-c4e3-5f5d-aa68-cfda38cab971" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048642}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529412 :question-generator/id #uuid "415c4d0e-413b-5fc2-8241-ef6a11198248" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186119887.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120071 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9283f0f3-aead-5a49-a589-fe4b9f0beadc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0, 4\\cos^{2} u, v\\cos u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116634} {:answer/id #uuid "ca24c4b4-3acf-5e8c-a05e-704e1bafe575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-4\\cos^{2} u, v\\cos u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116635} {:answer/id #uuid "05f0e7f4-6241-5d07-9f45-5f551087aa60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8v^{2}\\sin u,-4\\cos^{2} u, 2v\\cos u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116636} {:answer/id #uuid "2224c6b7-49bb-586f-8cb8-9afa3d02bd29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8v^{2}\\sin u, 4\\cos^{2} u, 2v\\cos u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116637} {:answer/id #uuid "7dc2b54e-bb7f-58fc-b1d2-67c4cfc8b260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\cos u, 0,-4v\\sin u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116638}] :answer-field/id #uuid "33515c78-97bb-5acf-ae0a-409b8db30f44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116633} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "669c4a14-f117-5445-b5bc-ddb0e9ee19d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386156} {:answer/id #uuid "eef920f4-e456-5f91-861d-e610778fc9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,2v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386157} {:answer/id #uuid "f3f56c70-5d40-5441-8d68-4c329568c111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,-4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386158} {:answer/id #uuid "f2243c43-9e9a-5017-9fb8-6ac7cf899ac8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,0,\\,-4v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386159} {:answer/id #uuid "9ff4ca66-39af-5179-9dd1-8d5dfc378981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,-4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,2v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ff4ca66-39af-5179-9dd1-8d5dfc378981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,-4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,2v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386160} :answer-field/id #uuid "a72c3135-50a8-5b65-947b-d6cde382e4fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf9a45d8-93e4-5a5c-8ad1-796e86ba6570" :question/math-academy-id "q-105606" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,{v}^{2},\\,4v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,0,\\,-4v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡u & 0 & -4v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 0 & 2v & 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -4v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 2v & 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & -4v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 0 & 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,-4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,2v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "982f0ab2-b067-5c6d-b436-f571911405c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨u\\cos u - 2v^{2}, v - u, 2v - \\cos u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116640} {:answer/id #uuid "c223a78d-a39f-5351-a8af-67883f6db74a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨u\\cos u, u - v, 2v - \\cos u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116641} {:answer/id #uuid "cefe9979-f81e-56ed-926e-600bdfe5460b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1, 2v, u - 2\\cos u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116642} {:answer/id #uuid "dc7f41be-726c-5f31-b256-d84fda88aa40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-2v + v\\sin u, u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116643} {:answer/id #uuid "7208d96c-0568-52be-8d8f-e2e9979410a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨u\\sin u - 2v^{2}, v - u, 2v - \\sin u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116644}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6cbd4bbf-1bba-55f3-a870-2233f91c7e89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116639}] :question/id #uuid "809dc595-ac5d-5204-a855-46578f8e39d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-105607" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations\n\n$x = u + v, y = v^{2} + \\sin u, z = uv$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b5fd3b7-f0ec-5c2c-9692-878483a3901c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b5fd3b7-f0ec-5c2c-9692-878483a3901c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234735} :answer-field/id #uuid "89c00608-1fd8-5842-87ec-284d501398aa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31e7ec00-583e-5e36-85bc-2752f04d085a" :question/math-academy-id "q-167648" :question/problem "Find the norm of the fundamental vector product for the surface $r(x,\\theta ),$ found in the previous step.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $‖{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}‖=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn part 4, we got the surface\n\n$$\nr(x,\\theta )=⟨x,\\,2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,x\\in [0,1],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\ {r}_{\\theta }^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂\\theta }(x),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂\\theta }(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂\\theta }(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0 & -2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ -2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0 & 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0 & -2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8{x}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +8{x}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ,\\,-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8{x}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ),\\,-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8{x}^{3},\\,-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding norm is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}‖ & =\\sqrt{(8{x}^{3})^{2}+(-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64{x}^{6}+4{x}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +4{x}^{4}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64{x}^{6}+4{x}^{4}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64{x}^{6}+4{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247058 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b01efda-a1d2-53e8-b5bc-b7b1a4bd597d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨u,\\,-2v,\\,u+v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244414} {:answer/id #uuid "0c73f40c-f1b5-55d4-9961-9039687ed039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨u,\\,u-2v,\\,v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244426} {:answer/id #uuid "a6bbcd41-38e7-55f7-ab59-08810647c06c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2u,\\,2v,\\,2u-2v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245805} {:answer/id #uuid "d0f7fbfe-e8d8-530a-9cdc-2f5a53c4a3a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2u,\\,2v,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246174} {:answer/id #uuid "d120b398-1642-5a8e-8cf2-53561f909c2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2u,\\,v+u,\\,2v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0f7fbfe-e8d8-530a-9cdc-2f5a53c4a3a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2u,\\,2v,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246174} :answer-field/id #uuid "94800350-4101-5013-898d-322c0bc8740a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246802}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e620e4a-e82b-57dd-8cd9-76c33846bfaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-109904" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y=v,\\,z={u}^{2}-{v}^{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2u \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2u \\\\ 1 & -2v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2u \\\\ 0 & -2v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u,\\,2v,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247059 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03dc8d10-95b3-5b5e-90c4-429e1a092d24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-v,\\,-{e}^{v},\\,{e}^{v}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244342} {:answer/id #uuid "2b0986bd-8324-5fc6-af83-5c7a0785be0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-{e}^{v},\\,-1,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244699} {:answer/id #uuid "3a0046d3-49c9-53cd-ab10-d95e7e800c8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨v,\\,-{e}^{v},\\,u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244828} {:answer/id #uuid "3dc8a714-c3ae-5552-91c2-4796e2474727" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-u,\\,{e}^{v},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244858} {:answer/id #uuid "d90a75f1-f422-53e5-aec0-6f1ff5b21547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,{e}^{v},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d90a75f1-f422-53e5-aec0-6f1ff5b21547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,{e}^{v},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246243} :answer-field/id #uuid "9766be27-1e6c-5bc6-87ca-c30306c27a20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dade4255-e1e8-5d68-9c25-815855912b22" :question/math-academy-id "q-109909" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y=v,\\,z=u-{e}^{v}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u-{e}^{v}⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-{e}^{v})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-{e}^{v})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-{e}^{v}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -{e}^{v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -{e}^{v}\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{v}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,{e}^{v},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247060 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "069dd5b2-e962-5702-9988-ab651ad9f559" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6{v}^{2},\\,-2u,\\,6u{v}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244367} {:answer/id #uuid "1c91d380-9df8-58e3-80e3-71321b52efcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨v,\\,-2u,\\,-3u{v}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244566} {:answer/id #uuid "35fc3340-574c-5b8c-b291-0d9105ef8e30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨u-v,\\,2u,\\,{v}^{2}-u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244792} {:answer/id #uuid "e68b3584-bd42-592e-8ce7-48290c8d0c9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{v}^{2}-u,\\,2v,\\,u{v}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246355} {:answer/id #uuid "f4783f39-b9aa-5dd6-9685-baa83dca2ca0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6{v}^{2}+u,\\,-2u+v,\\,6u{v}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "069dd5b2-e962-5702-9988-ab651ad9f559" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6{v}^{2},\\,-2u,\\,6u{v}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244367} :answer-field/id #uuid "3105a5f1-0988-53a7-8f54-a8761ead7692" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d08c35d-51cc-50ea-bb44-1ebd28104462" :question/math-academy-id "q-109911" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx={u}^{2}+1,\\,y={v}^{3}+1,\\,z=2u+v.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2}+1,\\,{v}^{3}+1,\\,2u+v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{3}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{3}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3{v}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3{v}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3{v}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6{v}^{2},\\,-2u,\\,6u{v}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386480 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2eb0d66e-3112-5fe9-9738-ced5916fa2ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-uv\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,-u\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386482} {:answer/id #uuid "6b6ca289-8138-5fe4-8821-842eff514232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨uv\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386483} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd5d613-7c38-5ab1-a95e-dc8f1bcd65f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386484} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb76098-74bd-5aba-a21c-e6b0f4774589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨uv\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,-v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386485} {:answer/id #uuid "4398883f-b1ac-5be7-9888-7adcf970ed54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v+uv\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4398883f-b1ac-5be7-9888-7adcf970ed54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v+uv\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386486} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4014425-a793-5c90-8901-fc3e45dbe1ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386481}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f52e90e-7be3-5f9c-9e1c-12885e700253" :question/math-academy-id "q-109912" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,-v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡v & -v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 0 & u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & -v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ 0 & u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v+uv\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529336 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3158d5a7-3a0d-564b-b6fb-2802c49578ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 48 v^{2},\\,- 12 u,\\,72 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529346} {:answer/id #uuid "4ebc0dc8-e1eb-526d-b156-67f24bff1e0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6 u,\\,0,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529352} {:answer/id #uuid "8f662bdf-3426-541b-aeae-8f73c454cac5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 48 v^{2},\\,12 u,\\,72 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529373} {:answer/id #uuid "9ac7215a-1e75-5bca-9b78-c47a51cd04cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨48 v^{2},\\,12 u,\\,- 72 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529377} {:answer/id #uuid "b7bf49b0-96d5-5f6a-bf2a-ab30c93bed0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,12 v^{2},\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3158d5a7-3a0d-564b-b6fb-2802c49578ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 48 v^{2},\\,- 12 u,\\,72 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529346} :answer-field/id #uuid "90974337-909a-5a06-b301-97712683285d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "079d695e-b3a6-59aa-920c-1ff665e1082b" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=3\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,y=4\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,z=2\\left(2u+v\\right).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨3\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,4\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,2\\left(2u+v\\right)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6 u,\\,0,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3\\left({u}^{2}\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,12 v^{2},\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 3\\left(2u\\right) & 0 & 2\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 4\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 2\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 4\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 2\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}3\\left(2u\\right) & 2\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 2\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}3\\left(2u\\right) & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right)\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 48 v^{2},\\,- 12 u,\\,72 u v^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529341 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "513c0ff2-0b40-5d28-ae4c-7dbd8c46d8e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 72 v^{2},\\,- 8 u,\\,18 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529353} {:answer/id #uuid "5ae97bc8-ceab-539c-b279-77e85c4ec979" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 72 v^{2},\\,8 u,\\,18 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529357} {:answer/id #uuid "707eea66-3c70-52f8-96ff-83c9270232ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2 u,\\,0,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529363} {:answer/id #uuid "e542ea0c-15b0-5e7c-bebb-9196a291740b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨72 v^{2},\\,8 u,\\,- 18 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529403} {:answer/id #uuid "f6825be3-48b8-58cc-a7e1-1b5a5360a776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,9 v^{2},\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "513c0ff2-0b40-5d28-ae4c-7dbd8c46d8e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 72 v^{2},\\,- 8 u,\\,18 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529353} :answer-field/id #uuid "17726b3e-da12-5100-9529-30dd30f97ab5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1f7b80e6-fd6c-56fc-be8d-0adb41e9046a" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx={u}^{2}+1,\\,y=3\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,z=4\\left(2u+v\\right).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2}+1,\\,3\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,4\\left(2u+v\\right)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,8⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,9 v^{2},\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 4\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 3\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 4\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 3\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 4\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 4\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 4\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right)\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 72 v^{2},\\,- 8 u,\\,18 u v^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529345 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e322d8-ea35-5e03-9ba3-b9169197298c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,6 v,\\,u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529335} {:answer/id #uuid "1f5939eb-96cb-569a-a36d-99edfcd63b12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3 u \\cos{(u )} - 6 v^{2},\\,- 2 u + 2 v,\\,12 v - 6 \\cos{(u )}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529340} {:answer/id #uuid "5d22a2bd-bcc3-592e-a7f6-40f9aab6f703" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3 u \\cos{(u )} - 6 v^{2},\\,2 u - 2 v,\\,12 v - 6 \\cos{(u )}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529358} {:answer/id #uuid "7a398103-fe6d-5bb1-982f-5e9709d919e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,3 \\cos{(u )},\\,v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529365} {:answer/id #uuid "f26aabe8-b114-5c96-bf02-8440e5209761" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 3 u \\cos{(u )} + 6 v^{2},\\,2 u - 2 v,\\,- 12 v + 6 \\cos{(u )}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f5939eb-96cb-569a-a36d-99edfcd63b12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3 u \\cos{(u )} - 6 v^{2},\\,- 2 u + 2 v,\\,12 v - 6 \\cos{(u )}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529340} :answer-field/id #uuid "46102bec-425d-5814-92d4-891a6a84571f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f1ae609-38a0-53f0-baa0-900f6821dc85" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations\n\n$x = 2\\left(u + v\\right), y = 3\\left(v^{2} + \\sin u\\right), z = uv$." :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2 u + 2 v,\\,3 v^{2} + 3 \\sin{(u )},\\,u v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 u + 2 v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3 v^{2} + 3 \\sin{(u )}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,3 \\cos{(u )},\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 u + 2 v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3 v^{2} + 3 \\sin{(u )}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,6 v,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 3 \\cos{(u )} & v \\\\ 2 & 6 v & u\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}3 \\cos{(u )} & v \\\\ 6 v & u\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & v \\\\ 2 & u\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\cos{(u )} \\\\ 2 & 6 v\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(3 \\cos{(u )})(u)-(v)(6 v),\\,-[(2)(u)-(v)(2)],\\,(2)(6 v)-(3 \\cos{(u )})(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3 u \\cos{(u )} - 6 v^{2},\\,- 2 u + 2 v,\\,12 v - 6 \\cos{(u )}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529348 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7302147c-799a-53fc-9de8-45d235aa655f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8 u,\\,0,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529364} {:answer/id #uuid "a2e3ac65-4e72-576b-81d3-83baa3c9e6d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨48 v^{2},\\,16 u,\\,- 96 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529379} {:answer/id #uuid "c311f11d-ff39-5e16-a7cd-305794bdafae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 48 v^{2},\\,- 16 u,\\,96 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529390} {:answer/id #uuid "d5132c66-a16e-5aaf-8021-9cfcf9dae875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 48 v^{2},\\,16 u,\\,96 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529399} {:answer/id #uuid "f82660ec-1d20-5f98-a30b-893b20483f22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,12 v^{2},\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c311f11d-ff39-5e16-a7cd-305794bdafae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 48 v^{2},\\,- 16 u,\\,96 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529390} :answer-field/id #uuid "97d1543c-ce7e-5c30-9e63-bcf33b02c1b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "34df8a07-4ac5-5db8-94ec-53489ab5c141" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=4\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,y=4\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,z=2\\left(2u+v\\right).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨4\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,4\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,2\\left(2u+v\\right)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8 u,\\,0,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4\\left({u}^{2}\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,12 v^{2},\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 4\\left(2u\\right) & 0 & 2\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 4\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 2\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 4\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 2\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}4\\left(2u\\right) & 2\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 2\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}4\\left(2u\\right) & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right)\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 48 v^{2},\\,- 16 u,\\,96 u v^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529356 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "678770cb-842e-5e05-b487-43b37e01953a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,\\,8 e^{v},\\,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529362} {:answer/id #uuid "7e92ad08-43c8-5f16-bc7c-2fba47afaa13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,0,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529367} {:answer/id #uuid "ac60ce9d-5cfc-5603-8b92-38ff4555d026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12,\\,- 8 e^{v},\\,-6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529382} {:answer/id #uuid "ae160852-fc16-5a75-97b8-496d8b57ecb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,3,\\,- 4 e^{v}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529383} {:answer/id #uuid "e811bfc6-8c6f-5dc9-955e-158552f9c970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,\\,- 8 e^{v},\\,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "678770cb-842e-5e05-b487-43b37e01953a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,\\,8 e^{v},\\,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529362} :answer-field/id #uuid "52fa7d03-36ca-5ec6-a545-028ec9a3e3b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529355}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "536925ac-3a11-5824-b56c-c42c0cb5a4dc" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=2\\left(u\\right),\\,y=3\\left(v\\right),\\,z=4\\left(u-{e}^{v}\\right).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2\\left(u\\right),\\,3\\left(v\\right),\\,4\\left(u-{e}^{v}\\right)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\left(u\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3\\left(v\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4\\left(u-{e}^{v}\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\left(u\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3\\left(v\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4\\left(u-{e}^{v}\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3,\\,- 4 e^{v}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2\\left(1\\right) & 0 & 4\\left(1\\right) \\\\ 0 & 3\\left(1\\right) & 4\\left(-{e}^{v}\\right)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4\\left(1\\right) \\\\ 3\\left(1\\right) & 4\\left(-{e}^{v}\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}2\\left(1\\right) & 4\\left(1\\right) \\\\ 0 & 4\\left(-{e}^{v}\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}2\\left(1\\right) & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-12,\\,8 e^{v},\\,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529359 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d0c0d85-2f02-55dc-9473-202a33fde613" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,\\sin{(v )},\\,- v \\sin{(u )}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529344} {:answer/id #uuid "3d18ed36-4dfa-5c0a-8d32-485072bbb2cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨u v \\sin{(u )} \\cos{(v )} + \\sin{(v )} \\cos{(u )},\\,- 3 \\cos{(u )},\\,3 u \\cos{(v )}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529349} {:answer/id #uuid "a2a95bff-92b9-53c6-8fe5-0f0d43b2da54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,u \\cos{(v )},\\,\\cos{(u )}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529378} {:answer/id #uuid "d47bf98b-95ef-5c6e-a01e-21e1f47b6e49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- u v \\sin{(u )} \\cos{(v )} - \\sin{(v )} \\cos{(u )},\\,3 \\cos{(u )},\\,- 3 u \\cos{(v )}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529398} {:answer/id #uuid "e687c503-1567-58df-be9a-1878259734e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨u v \\sin{(u )} \\cos{(v )} + \\sin{(v )} \\cos{(u )},\\,3 \\cos{(u )},\\,3 u \\cos{(v )}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d18ed36-4dfa-5c0a-8d32-485072bbb2cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨u v \\sin{(u )} \\cos{(v )} + \\sin{(v )} \\cos{(u )},\\,- 3 \\cos{(u )},\\,3 u \\cos{(v )}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529349} :answer-field/id #uuid "f47863d9-76b7-508b-9a8f-b6a3c48353d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5f82fba6-89f1-5c94-8cc8-c031a913d71e" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨3\\left(u\\right),\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3\\left(u\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,-v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3\\left(u\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 3\\left(1\\right) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡v & -v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 0 & u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & -v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}3\\left(1\\right) & -v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}3\\left(1\\right) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ 0 & u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v+uv\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,- 3 \\cos{(u )},\\,3 u \\cos{(v )}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c963dd3-a1f9-5682-99a3-17ca99265979" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨9 u \\cos{(u )} - 18 v^{2},\\,9 u - 9 v,\\,18 v - 9 \\cos{(u )}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529366} {:answer/id #uuid "948274ad-00c2-576b-8a46-9c49f17fea14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 9 u \\cos{(u )} + 18 v^{2},\\,9 u - 9 v,\\,- 18 v + 9 \\cos{(u )}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529375} {:answer/id #uuid "af4abca4-9c9c-5890-99b9-eab3686e51f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,6 v,\\,3 u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529384} {:answer/id #uuid "c99438fc-2a5a-57e6-8a6f-35fd0cb40dad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨9 u \\cos{(u )} - 18 v^{2},\\,- 9 u + 9 v,\\,18 v - 9 \\cos{(u )}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529392} {:answer/id #uuid "ccaccd12-671f-52c4-8b18-a8e1d1b6a31c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,3 \\cos{(u )},\\,3 v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c99438fc-2a5a-57e6-8a6f-35fd0cb40dad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨9 u \\cos{(u )} - 18 v^{2},\\,- 9 u + 9 v,\\,18 v - 9 \\cos{(u )}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529392} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cf26bf8-7ae2-5ac3-aef1-b50aa10ab485" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a36ce165-471f-570d-9650-640cec5623fe" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations\n\n$x = 3\\left(u + v\\right), y = 3\\left(v^{2} + \\sin u\\right), z = 3\\left(uv\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨3 u + 3 v,\\,3 v^{2} + 3 \\sin{(u )},\\,3 u v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3 u + 3 v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3 v^{2} + 3 \\sin{(u )}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3 u v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,3 \\cos{(u )},\\,3 v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3 u + 3 v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3 v^{2} + 3 \\sin{(u )}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3 u v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,6 v,\\,3 u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 3 \\cos{(u )} & 3 v \\\\ 3 & 6 v & 3 u\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}3 \\cos{(u )} & 3 v \\\\ 6 v & 3 u\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 3 v \\\\ 3 & 3 u\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 3 \\cos{(u )} \\\\ 3 & 6 v\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(3 \\cos{(u )})(3 u)-(3 v)(6 v),\\,-[(3)(3 u)-(3 v)(3)],\\,(3)(6 v)-(3 \\cos{(u )})(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9 u \\cos{(u )} - 18 v^{2},\\,- 9 u + 9 v,\\,18 v - 9 \\cos{(u )}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529385 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "517f96df-2944-53eb-b50d-17f1387e43ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨72 v^{2},\\,16 u,\\,- 36 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529354} {:answer/id #uuid "64e9e700-d3cd-54f5-b9b2-d40f9cb5c9d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4 u,\\,0,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529360} {:answer/id #uuid "6685d10d-ae48-537c-b0e4-0a386d10674a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 72 v^{2},\\,16 u,\\,36 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529361} {:answer/id #uuid "8352b7c2-83f1-5e9d-9d58-b6ea2e141b52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 72 v^{2},\\,- 16 u,\\,36 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529368} {:answer/id #uuid "d39e64d9-d1b0-54f3-8894-9323b7b1df99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,9 v^{2},\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8352b7c2-83f1-5e9d-9d58-b6ea2e141b52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 72 v^{2},\\,- 16 u,\\,36 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529368} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc616a45-3e00-5d64-b7a9-e4fced4e40f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529401}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "afa8c161-9dec-5962-a3c6-b42a56e57915" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=2\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,y=3\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,z=4\\left(2u+v\\right).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,3\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,4\\left(2u+v\\right)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4 u,\\,0,\\,8⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\left({u}^{2}\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,9 v^{2},\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2\\left(2u\\right) & 0 & 4\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 3\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 4\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 3\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 4\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}2\\left(2u\\right) & 4\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 4\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}2\\left(2u\\right) & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right)\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 72 v^{2},\\,- 16 u,\\,36 u v^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529391 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2175fd76-0c56-57b8-9174-0002272778f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,3,\\,- 4 e^{v}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529342} {:answer/id #uuid "23fff28c-98c6-517d-894e-e3ade0b85cc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,\\,4 e^{v},\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529343} {:answer/id #uuid "bef9218d-e0fe-5ce0-82f9-bf47cfd7d97b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12,\\,- 4 e^{v},\\,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529389} {:answer/id #uuid "d62667d1-734a-5e83-a94c-519d0e08464a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,\\,- 4 e^{v},\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529400} {:answer/id #uuid "e8db9f02-5e58-5d77-9a53-681489b491a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,0,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23fff28c-98c6-517d-894e-e3ade0b85cc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,\\,4 e^{v},\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529343} :answer-field/id #uuid "4775f4af-3673-54e1-9229-30258922e843" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c43bafbb-27d1-589d-9395-34d1fb53b842" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y=3\\left(v\\right),\\,z=4\\left(u-{e}^{v}\\right).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,3\\left(v\\right),\\,4\\left(u-{e}^{v}\\right)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3\\left(v\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4\\left(u-{e}^{v}\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3\\left(v\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4\\left(u-{e}^{v}\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3,\\,- 4 e^{v}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\left(1\\right) \\\\ 0 & 3\\left(1\\right) & 4\\left(-{e}^{v}\\right)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4\\left(1\\right) \\\\ 3\\left(1\\right) & 4\\left(-{e}^{v}\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4\\left(1\\right) \\\\ 0 & 4\\left(-{e}^{v}\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-12,\\,4 e^{v},\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529402 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c01696f-1313-569d-b8dd-1b6ab93e698b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 12 v^{2},\\,- 12 u,\\,18 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529339} {:answer/id #uuid "328d5447-3347-5040-9526-4d0f97f066b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12 v^{2},\\,12 u,\\,- 18 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529347} {:answer/id #uuid "8957384e-fa9c-5800-9b29-602d86892550" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 12 v^{2},\\,12 u,\\,18 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529370} {:answer/id #uuid "bc6fc1db-b13a-5b17-a1ee-f3152ebb05c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6 u,\\,0,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529388} {:answer/id #uuid "d022c4c7-0c21-5bf5-99c0-d849f94827ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,3 v^{2},\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c01696f-1313-569d-b8dd-1b6ab93e698b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 12 v^{2},\\,- 12 u,\\,18 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529339} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb049baa-bb14-5762-b5a8-0e6bb3e655ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e182b79a-69d6-51fa-bb1c-78fc47b34b3a" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=3\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,y={v}^{3}+1,\\,z=2\\left(2u+v\\right).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨3\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,{v}^{3}+1,\\,2\\left(2u+v\\right)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{3}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6 u,\\,0,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3\\left({u}^{2}\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{3}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\left(2u+v\\right))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3{v}^{2},\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 3\\left(2u\\right) & 0 & 2\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 3{v}^{2} & 2\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 3{v}^{2} & 2\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}3\\left(2u\\right) & 2\\left(2\\right) \\\\ 0 & 2\\left(1\\right)\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}3\\left(2u\\right) & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3{v}^{2}\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 12 v^{2},\\,- 12 u,\\,18 u v^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529409 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "893aedc5-d336-51fd-a323-6bc046fac648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8 u,\\,0,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529369} {:answer/id #uuid "8d182813-aebd-50d7-b3b8-2aae19e921af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12 v^{2},\\,8 u,\\,- 48 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529372} {:answer/id #uuid "a76d51bc-cc84-5183-8de3-86672a302969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 12 v^{2},\\,- 8 u,\\,48 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529381} {:answer/id #uuid "b7590c8f-53c2-5e60-abe5-94dba4b54823" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,6 v^{2},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529386} {:answer/id #uuid "cf34330c-97e2-5157-b920-b9f0ebafbfa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 12 v^{2},\\,8 u,\\,48 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a76d51bc-cc84-5183-8de3-86672a302969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- 12 v^{2},\\,- 8 u,\\,48 u v^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529381} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a9644d7-6a0d-58f4-8f95-fffe69d2cb42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5c049c6-8f99-5422-a42e-c9b464f4ec2b" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=4\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,y=2\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,z=2u+v.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨4\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right),\\,2\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right),\\,2u+v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4\\left({u}^{2}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8 u,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4\\left({u}^{2}\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\left({v}^{3}+1\\right)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,6 v^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 4\\left(2u\\right) & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right) & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}4\\left(2u\\right) & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}4\\left(2u\\right) & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\left(3{v}^{2}\\right)\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 12 v^{2},\\,- 8 u,\\,48 u v^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Fundamental Vector Product of a Parametric Surface"}]}
